  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Social Cohesion and Building Trust between the Police and the Population through Community Policing, Democratic Dialogue and Economic Recovery in Kasai Province</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project led by IOM, in partnership with UNDP and UN Women, seeks to remedy the different drivers of insecurity through the combination of a community policing approach, democratic dialogue and economic recovery. The project&apos;s intervention strategy is part of an inclusive and participatory approach aimed at ensuring the participation of populations and security actors in issues related to security governance. In particular, through this project, IOM aims at addressing the structural and underlying causes of conflict by seeking to address the current security vacuum, the strengthening of trust between the population and State actors and the strengthening of community resilience through the development of sustainable socio-economic opportunities, particularly for those most vulnerable.</narrative>
  </description>
